<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37076" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pŏpŭlōsus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		1. populus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>abounding in people</i>, <i>populous</i>, <i>numerous</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gens populosa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Flor. p. 342</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">familia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. M. 5, p. 162</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Briareus populoso corpore,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Carm. 15, 27</span></i>
			.—<i>Comp.</i>: populosior globus,
			Veg.Mil. 3, 19 <i>fin.—Sup.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insula populosissima,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 52</span></i>
			.</div>
